1573
01:11:14.660 --> 01:11:16.970
to the press but doesn't that need to be reasonable

1574
01:11:16.970 --> 01:11:19.480
and within certain parameters and can't we respect

1575
01:11:20.323 --> 01:11:22.364
the sovereignty of the athlete

1576
01:11:22.364 --> 01:11:24.370
when they say enough is enough.

1577
01:11:24.370 --> 01:11:27.650
Yeah probably all the social media

1578
01:11:27.650 --> 01:11:31.700
changes the dynamics of sports.

1579
01:11:31.700 --> 01:11:34.000
What is your approach to social media

1580
01:11:34.000 --> 01:11:36.360
like do you feel like you need to be sharing stuff

1581
01:11:36.360 --> 01:11:38.110
and you've got sponsors

1582
01:11:38.110 --> 01:11:41.720
and people that want you to be kind of out there

1583
01:11:41.720 --> 01:11:42.553
in that way.

1584
01:11:43.960 --> 01:11:48.400
Yeah I mean I'm sort of I feel sort of new to it still

1585
01:11:49.460 --> 01:11:52.800
but I just it's a cool way to connect with people

1586
01:11:52.800 --> 01:11:55.073
is how I view it and so like,

1587
01:11:55.930 --> 01:11:59.550
I am having fun sharing my story using it

1588
01:11:59.550 --> 01:12:02.710
because maybe it can connect with someone who

1589
01:12:03.970 --> 01:12:06.220
maybe it helps them try something hard

1590
01:12:07.260 --> 01:12:10.670
I don't know and I mean my sponsors are fantastic

1591
01:12:10.670 --> 01:12:14.450
so I don't have pressure from them to like

1592
01:12:14.450 --> 01:12:16.020
do a certain thing or.

1593
01:12:16.020 --> 01:12:19.310
Yeah Salomon is your main sponsor.

1594
01:12:19.310 --> 01:12:20.143
That's correct.

1595
01:12:20.143 --> 01:12:22.450
Yeah you know I just joined the Salomon team

1596
01:12:22.450 --> 01:12:23.977
I'm so excited.

1597
01:12:23.977 --> 01:12:25.140
Now we gotta go running.
I think we're gonna

1598
01:12:25.140 --> 01:12:26.310
announce it tomorrow.

1599
01:12:26.310 --> 01:12:28.820
I'm super excited about it.

1600
01:12:28.820 --> 01:12:32.260
No it's hilarious like oh joining the Salomon family

1601
01:12:32.260 --> 01:12:34.470
I'm like with people like Courtney

1602
01:12:34.470 --> 01:12:36.810
like I don't like I'm way in the back like

1603
01:12:36.810 --> 01:12:38.700
I can't even believe that I'm here but

1604
01:12:38.700 --> 01:12:40.560
I'm really excited about it

1605
01:12:40.560 --> 01:12:43.920
and I love all the people that I've met

1606
01:12:43.920 --> 01:12:45.840
and gotten to spend a little bit of time with

1607
01:12:45.840 --> 01:12:50.570
and everything is just so dialed in and super pro

1608
01:12:50.570 --> 01:12:52.830
from the gear to just the integrity

1609
01:12:52.830 --> 01:12:55.760
and it's been really it's like a dream come true for me.

1610
01:12:55.760 --> 01:12:57.030
Oh that's so cool.

1611
01:12:57.030 --> 01:12:59.510
So Aaron and Juris were supposed to come out

1612
01:12:59.510 --> 01:13:01.500
and do the Iron Cowboy thing with me the other day

1613
01:13:01.500 --> 01:13:04.060
but their young end wasn't feeling well

1614
01:13:04.060 --> 01:13:05.150
so they couldn't do it but

1615
01:13:05.150 --> 01:13:07.180
I was hoping to see them on Saturday.

1616
01:13:07.180 --> 01:13:08.013
They're so great.

1617
01:13:08.013 --> 01:13:09.290
Yeah.
I'm so pumped

1618
01:13:09.290 --> 01:13:10.210
you're on the team.

1619
01:13:10.210 --> 01:13:12.690
I know I should figure out some kind of

1620
01:13:12.690 --> 01:13:16.180
I feel like I have I really have to live up.

1621
01:13:16.180 --> 01:13:17.359
No.

1622
01:13:17.359 --> 01:13:19.100
(both laughs)

1623
01:13:19.100 --> 01:13:21.820
I got to find some kind of challenge for myself

1624
01:13:21.820 --> 01:13:25.196
or whatever to legitimize the relationship.

1625
01:13:25.196 --> 01:13:26.480
I'm really proud,

1626
01:13:26.480 --> 01:13:27.555
I'm really proud.
What would it be?

1627
01:13:27.555 --> 01:13:29.480
Would you want to do a Backyard race?

1628
01:13:29.480 --> 01:13:32.310
Maybe I have to put in quite a bit of work

1629
01:13:32.310 --> 01:13:35.230
between now and maybe in a year I have to get ready

1630
01:13:35.230 --> 01:13:36.110
I gotta heal my back up.

1631
01:13:36.110 --> 01:13:39.263
If you had to choose between a Backyard or a 200.

1632
01:13:40.848 --> 01:13:42.480
I think I can wrap my head around a Backyard.

1633
01:13:42.480 --> 01:13:45.300
Yeah that's what's cool about it is that

1634
01:13:45.300 --> 01:13:48.750
it can be as as hard as your body is able to go, right?

1635
01:13:48.750 --> 01:13:52.413
And those little breaks become super significant.

1636
01:13:54.560 --> 01:13:57.480
And mentally it's not as intimidating.

1637
01:13:57.480 --> 01:14:00.293
Yeah it is a cool format I mean,

1638
01:14:01.510 --> 01:14:04.520
the first year I was there I think,

1639
01:14:04.520 --> 01:14:06.690
there was a person who was like.

1640
01:14:06.690 --> 01:14:10.080
I'm just gonna try to run my first marathon ever today

1641
01:14:10.080 --> 01:14:13.670
and they wanted to stay in to get their 26 miles

1642
01:14:13.670 --> 01:14:15.700
and then they were gonna feel satisfied

1643
01:14:15.700 --> 01:14:19.530
and they ended up doing I think 100k like 62 miles

1644
01:14:19.530 --> 01:14:23.200
because four miles at a time they just kept thinking like

1645
01:14:23.200 --> 01:14:25.453
oh I can do one more, I can do one more.

1646
01:14:26.790 --> 01:14:29.080
Yeah I think the the Goggins challenge

1647
01:14:29.080 --> 01:14:33.290
where he did the four by four by 48 was a similar thing

1648
01:14:33.290 --> 01:14:35.870
because it feels bite-sized

1649
01:14:35.870 --> 01:14:38.210
and you don't realize that it's actually hard

1650
01:14:38.210 --> 01:14:39.810
when you think about it until you're

1651
01:14:39.810 --> 01:14:42.260
actually doing it and you're in the middle of the night

1652
01:14:42.260 --> 01:14:43.093
Right.

1653
01:14:43.093 --> 01:14:46.120
And it encourages people to try something that maybe

1654
01:14:46.120 --> 01:14:48.440
they would have been too intimidated to do

1655
01:14:48.440 --> 01:14:50.600
if it was signing up for like a really long race.

1656
01:14:50.600 --> 01:14:52.350
Yeah absolutely.

1657
01:14:52.350 --> 01:14:55.470
Yeah I wanna think of something

1658
01:14:55.470 --> 01:14:58.070
like create my own thing though too

1659
01:14:58.070 --> 01:14:59.790
like I think there's something cool about that

1660
01:14:59.790 --> 01:15:04.180
and if there was a silver lining

1661
01:15:05.258 --> 01:15:08.670
to the pandemic with respect to ultras

1662
01:15:08.670 --> 01:15:13.140
it was the like Backyard, the Backyard challenge thing

1663
01:15:13.140 --> 01:15:16.100
that was was Mike Wardian the one who created that

1664
01:15:16.100 --> 01:15:18.110
he's the one who went the furthest.

1665
01:15:18.110 --> 01:15:19.213
To do the virtual Backyard.

1666
01:15:19.213 --> 01:15:20.504
Yeah the virtual thing.

1667
01:15:20.504 --> 01:15:22.260
Yeah went the furthest

1668
01:15:22.260 --> 01:15:25.780
he was our Dave Proctor and his team in Canada

1669
01:15:25.780 --> 01:15:28.053
who like put together the event.

1670
01:15:29.400 --> 01:15:30.840
Yeah those things are cool.

1671
01:15:30.840 --> 01:15:31.940
Yeah.

1672
01:15:31.940 --> 01:15:33.183
To be able to create community

1673
01:15:33.183 --> 01:15:34.820
when we couldn't be together.

1674
01:15:34.820 --> 01:15:36.690
Yeah oh it was so fun.

1675
01:15:36.690 --> 01:15:37.523
Well I know.

1676
01:15:37.523 --> 01:15:39.430
It felt like we were all hanging out together

1677
01:15:39.430 --> 01:15:41.187
even though I was just staring at this little screen.

1678
01:15:41.187 --> 01:15:42.893
I know right I know.

1679
01:15:44.330 --> 01:15:46.040
Well it must be nice to feel like you can

1680
01:15:46.040 --> 01:15:49.160
start traveling now and the world is opening up a little bit

1681
01:15:49.160 --> 01:15:51.720
and all that.
Yeah it feels awesome.

1682
01:15:51.720 --> 01:15:56.410
Like seeing people doing things I think though like

1683
01:15:57.270 --> 01:15:58.690
I kind of liked last year

1684
01:15:58.690 --> 01:16:02.840
and like finding appreciation in these trails

1685
01:16:02.840 --> 01:16:04.970
that were right out my door all the time

1686
01:16:04.970 --> 01:16:09.970
that I had gotten taking them for granted basically

1687
01:16:10.030 --> 01:16:12.810
and then being stuck at home all last Spring

1688
01:16:12.810 --> 01:16:14.690
and into the Summer it was like

1689
01:16:14.690 --> 01:16:16.100
oh there's a lot of cool link-ups

1690
01:16:16.100 --> 01:16:19.120
you can actually make if you're just looking for it.

1691
01:16:19.120 --> 01:16:21.793
Right it encouraged you to explore a little bit more.

1692
01:16:21.793 --> 01:16:24.640
Yeah and I saw way more families out on the trails

1693
01:16:24.640 --> 01:16:26.760
and just getting outside more so

1694
01:16:26.760 --> 01:16:29.880
I think it could have some cool things come from it

1695
01:16:29.880 --> 01:16:32.800
even though it was definitely not great.

1696
01:16:32.800 --> 01:16:36.020
Amelia Boone lives in Golden also doesn't she

1697
01:16:36.020 --> 01:16:37.430
do you ever go running with her.

1698
01:16:37.430 --> 01:16:42.430
No I saw her during a virtual run I was doing

1699
01:16:42.810 --> 01:16:44.860
and we crossed paths on the trails

1700
01:16:44.860 --> 01:16:47.160
but otherwise we haven't run together.

1701
01:16:47.160 --> 01:16:49.380
Really didn't you but one of the

1702
01:16:49.380 --> 01:16:54.380
'cause the the the Backyard Ultra you do it in teams right?

1703
01:16:54.830 --> 01:16:56.850
That like the the U.S. has their team

1704
01:16:56.850 --> 01:16:59.330
and there was like wasn't Amelia part of one teams?

1705
01:16:59.330 --> 01:17:04.330
Yeah so we that was in person at in Tennessee in the Fall

1706
01:17:04.770 --> 01:17:07.100
we were able to share a ton of miles there

1707
01:17:08.090 --> 01:17:10.040
but never in Golden.

1708
01:17:10.040 --> 01:17:14.030
That's so that's funny yeah I feel like I had this

1709
01:17:14.030 --> 01:17:16.340
idea like oh you guys are like hanging out and running

1710
01:17:16.340 --> 01:17:18.310
and having coffee and doing stuff like that

1711
01:17:18.310 --> 01:17:21.220
all the time no.

1712
01:17:21.220 --> 01:17:23.630
No not recently, we should.

1713
01:17:23.630 --> 01:17:28.630
What is the ultra running community of the future

1714
01:17:28.700 --> 01:17:29.940
that you would like to see like

1715
01:17:29.940 --> 01:17:33.530
where is all this heading and like explain to somebody

1716
01:17:33.530 --> 01:17:37.130
who's listening or watching who's unfamiliar with this world

1717
01:17:37.130 --> 01:17:39.200
like what's great about it

1718
01:17:39.200 --> 01:17:44.143
and why maybe they should think of stepping into it.

1719
01:17:45.800 --> 01:17:50.530
Oh man so many reasons just exploring with your feet

1720
01:17:50.530 --> 01:17:54.800
like the places you end up with just your body

1721
01:17:54.800 --> 01:17:56.930
carrying you there is pretty cool

1722
01:17:56.930 --> 01:18:00.690
and it feels special to be in the middle of nowhere

1723
01:18:00.690 --> 01:18:04.260
and to have gotten yourself there on purpose.

1724
01:18:04.260 --> 01:18:06.470
I think it's the most welcoming community

1725
01:18:06.470 --> 01:18:10.380
my the first 50-mile race I did one of the things was

1726
01:18:10.380 --> 01:18:14.350
that hooked me was how awesome the people around me were

1727
01:18:14.350 --> 01:18:19.010
and I mean we were in hail and sleet and just awful weather

1728
01:18:19.010 --> 01:18:23.050
and people were wearing garbage bags as their raincoats

1729
01:18:23.050 --> 01:18:25.220
because it kept them a little bit warmer

1730
01:18:25.220 --> 01:18:28.850
and all signs pointed to like we should

1731
01:18:28.850 --> 01:18:30.390
be hating life right now

1732
01:18:30.390 --> 01:18:32.433
but people were just making the best of it

1733
01:18:32.433 --> 01:18:36.480
they were hooping and hollering, splashing through puddles

1734
01:18:36.480 --> 01:18:39.060
finding like all the joy they could

1735
01:18:39.060 --> 01:18:41.584
in this miserable situation

1736
01:18:41.584 --> 01:18:46.584
and they're also the most helpful because in that same race

1737
01:18:47.200 --> 01:18:50.070
I face planted in a mud puddle

1738
01:18:50.070 --> 01:18:54.470
and a person 15 yards ahead ran back offered their hand

1739
01:18:54.470 --> 01:18:57.900
and pulled me out of this puddle to keep running together

1740
01:18:57.900 --> 01:18:59.650
like where does that happen?

1741
01:18:59.650 --> 01:19:00.483
Yeah.

1742
01:19:00.483 --> 01:19:01.960
You went out of your way to help me

1743
01:19:01.960 --> 01:19:04.951
it's not just that I was conveniently in your way

1744
01:19:04.951 --> 01:19:07.403
like they turned around and came back for me.

1745
01:19:07.403 --> 01:19:09.570
Yeah that is something really unique

1746
01:19:09.570 --> 01:19:11.327
about the community I think.

1747
01:19:11.327 --> 01:19:13.410
And I find that in every race

1748
01:19:13.410 --> 01:19:15.120
I mean everyone's ready to help

1749
01:19:15.120 --> 01:19:17.720
if you're on the side of the trail having trouble

1750
01:19:17.720 --> 01:19:20.800
like everyone who goes by is going to ask

1751
01:19:20.800 --> 01:19:24.515
what can I do how can I help you to get back on track.

1752
01:19:24.515 --> 01:19:28.130
And you might even hallucinate and you could go blind.

1753
01:19:28.130 --> 01:19:30.821
Yeah also perks.

1754
01:19:30.821 --> 01:19:32.170
(both laughing)

1755
01:19:32.170 --> 01:19:33.980
Can we talk about the hallucinations.

1756
01:19:33.980 --> 01:19:35.240
Have you ever hallucinated.

1757
01:19:35.240 --> 01:19:36.640
No.

1758
01:19:36.640 --> 01:19:39.620
Yeah it's fun you make some good friends.

1759
01:19:39.620 --> 01:19:42.920
Yeah I like your it's for me

1760
01:19:42.920 --> 01:19:45.020
I mean you hear lots of stories of ultra

1761
01:19:45.020 --> 01:19:47.690
runners having hallucinations

1762
01:19:47.690 --> 01:19:50.460
but what I love about your hallucinations

1763
01:19:50.460 --> 01:19:53.050
is your relationship to them like they're like your friends

1764
01:19:53.050 --> 01:19:56.320
or something like you're like oh this is awesome

1765
01:19:56.320 --> 01:19:59.430
there's Mickey Mouse over there doing whatever like

1766
01:19:59.430 --> 01:20:00.500
what is going on.

1767
01:20:00.500 --> 01:20:03.290
Mickey Mouse was throwing out T-shirts to the crowd

1768
01:20:03.290 --> 01:20:05.768
and he did not throw me one.

1769
01:20:05.768 --> 01:20:07.380
(Courtney laughs)

1770
01:20:07.380 --> 01:20:09.210
Do you know they're not real when they're happening

1771
01:20:09.210 --> 01:20:10.520
so there's a detachment

1772
01:20:11.467 --> 01:20:13.200
or are you thinking this is really real

1773
01:20:13.200 --> 01:20:16.560
and it's still cool for the most part now I can tell

1774
01:20:16.560 --> 01:20:19.180
they're not real there are some instances

1775
01:20:19.180 --> 01:20:22.840
where I have to like take double or triple takes

1776
01:20:22.840 --> 01:20:26.130
at something because I can't believe I'm seeing these

1777
01:20:26.130 --> 01:20:29.143
people dancing right there and like what are they doing.

1778
01:20:30.200 --> 01:20:32.870
But usually I can recognize it's not real

1779
01:20:32.870 --> 01:20:36.300
and it means that I'm doing something really cool

1780
01:20:36.300 --> 01:20:41.188
because these friends don't just come out anytime.

1781
01:20:41.188 --> 01:20:42.590
Right it's special.

1782
01:20:42.590 --> 01:20:43.850
Yeah.
Here they come,

1783
01:20:43.850 --> 01:20:44.870
do you know it's always gonna

1784
01:20:44.870 --> 01:20:46.770
happen at hour or whatever.

1785
01:20:46.770 --> 01:20:48.510
It's not a certain hour but it's

1786
01:20:49.420 --> 01:20:52.420
definitely over 24 hours of effort

1787
01:20:52.420 --> 01:20:57.420
and then like night time for sure brings out more friends.

1788
01:20:57.660 --> 01:21:01.300
So like UTMB starts in the evening

1789
01:21:01.300 --> 01:21:03.950
and so the night is when you're a little bit fresher

1790
01:21:03.950 --> 01:21:07.712
and so I made no friends at UTMB because.

1791
01:21:07.712 --> 01:21:08.880
You're like where are my friends.

1792
01:21:08.880 --> 01:21:13.640
Yeah even though that course would be hard enough

1793
01:21:13.640 --> 01:21:16.000
and take long enough where I maybe I would have made them

1794
01:21:16.000 --> 01:21:18.593
if the night had been at the end section.

1795
01:21:21.730 --> 01:21:24.750
I think you're a very healthy person I'm no shrink

1796
01:21:24.750 --> 01:21:28.810
but I think the the the sort of good-natured aspect

1797
01:21:28.810 --> 01:21:31.600
of your hallucinations speak to somebody

1798
01:21:31.600 --> 01:21:33.800
who's you know a very grounded individual

1799
01:21:33.800 --> 01:21:36.140
like if it was a lot of demons coming out at night

1800
01:21:36.140 --> 01:21:39.237
and people trying to kill you and stuff like

1801
01:21:39.237 --> 01:21:41.870
I feel like you should write them all down

1802
01:21:41.870 --> 01:21:46.130
and then you could give that journal to a psychiatrist

1803
01:21:46.130 --> 01:21:47.420
and say tell me who I am.

1804
01:21:47.420 --> 01:21:50.540
Yeah I don't know if I want them to analyze it

1805
01:21:50.540 --> 01:21:54.960
but I had to my friend Maggie who does Big's Backyard

1806
01:21:54.960 --> 01:21:58.160
and all sorts of adventures she has really scary ones

1807
01:21:58.160 --> 01:22:00.280
like she sees like heads on spears

1808
01:22:00.280 --> 01:22:01.767
and clowns and stuff.
Right.

1809
01:22:01.767 --> 01:22:05.140
I'm like Maggie you gotta watch happy movies

1810
01:22:05.140 --> 01:22:07.857
the day before like she's watching IT

1811
01:22:07.857 --> 01:22:09.748
the night before a race.

1812
01:22:09.748 --> 01:22:10.581
Yeah Annabelle

1813
01:22:10.581 --> 01:22:13.015
Yeah I'm like what do you think you're gonna see?

1814
01:22:13.015 --> 01:22:13.848
(Courtney laughs)

1815
01:22:13.848 --> 01:22:17.340
That's funny what about the blindness though.

1816
01:22:17.340 --> 01:22:20.050
Explain that story for people that don't know it.

1817
01:22:20.050 --> 01:22:21.973
Yeah I don't recommend it,

1818
01:22:23.410 --> 01:22:26.200
but what happened was it was a 100 mile race

1819
01:22:26.200 --> 01:22:28.630
and about 12 miles from the finish my vision

1820
01:22:28.630 --> 01:22:31.370
was just getting really foggy on the edges.

1821
01:22:31.370 --> 01:22:33.190
I thought it was my contact lenses

1822
01:22:33.190 --> 01:22:35.690
I thought it was my headlamp dying

1823
01:22:35.690 --> 01:22:37.580
like I couldn't figure out what was going on

1824
01:22:37.580 --> 01:22:41.260
but I for sure noticed I was seeing less and less

1825
01:22:41.260 --> 01:22:44.950
and by 10 miles out from the finish line

1826
01:22:44.950 --> 01:22:48.510
it just had closed in all the way where it was pure white

1827
01:22:48.510 --> 01:22:50.410
in my field of vision.

1828
01:22:50.410 --> 01:22:52.140
Like I waved my hand in front of my face

1829
01:22:52.140 --> 01:22:53.623
